<title>JAPAN: Toyoda Automatic shares bid-only in early Tokyo.</title>
<headline>Toyoda Automatic shares bid-only in early Tokyo.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Toyoda Automatic Loom Works Ltd were bid-only in early Tokyo morning trade on Thursday on news that it would buy back up to 10 billion yen worth of its own shares, traders said.</p>
<p>As of 0016 GMT, the shares were bid-only at 2,220 yen, compared with their Wednesday close of 2,180 yen.  </p>
<p>The maker of industrial machinery said on Wednesday that further details of the buy-back plan would be determined at the next board meeting.</p>
<p>Toyoda also announced on Wednesday that it would raise its annual dividend payout to a total of 16 yen per share for 1996/97, compared with an actual dividend of 13 yen a year before.</p>
